From: Retrorerr <116828772+Retrorerr@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: packagejob: run Update jobs only on the pool thread

PackageJobThread already queues update() for QThreadPool, but the
PackageJob constructor also called it directly, so every Update job ran
twice and the first run blocked the caller's thread. KNewStuff installs
every store item through PackageJob::update(), and a global theme
installs its dependencies by running knshandler and waiting for each
one, so System Settings' GUI thread froze until all of them finished.
Under PRoot an icon theme dependency (40k+ files and links) takes
30 s or more and KWin marks the window Not Responding.

Leave the work to the pooled run, like Install and Uninstall.
---
diff --git a/src/kpackage/packagejob.cpp b/src/kpackage/packagejob.cpp
--- a/src/kpackage/packagejob.cpp
+++ b/src/kpackage/packagejob.cpp
@@ -73,7 +73,6 @@ PackageJob::PackageJob(OperationType type, const Package &package, const QString
         setupNotificationsOnJobFinished(QStringLiteral("packageInstalled"));
     } else if (type == Update) {
         setupNotificationsOnJobFinished(QStringLiteral("packageUpdated"));
-        d->thread->update(src, dest, package);
     } else if (type == Uninstall) {
         setupNotificationsOnJobFinished(QStringLiteral("packageUninstalled"));
